{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1237002-2e-setting-hack-werewolf-the-curse","id":1237002,"title":"[2E Setting Hack] Werewolf: The Curse","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-19T20:34:46-07:00","id":1237002,"title":"[2E Setting Hack] Werewolf: The Curse","content":"Hail friends.<br /> <br /> I've been playing Werewolf the Forsaken for a long time and I have a lot of things I like about it and a lot of things I dislike about it. There are things I've had fun with but want to set aside, and things I've never tried but want to. Therefore, because I have too much time, I have created a setting hack that changes some of the focus from the original game from 'Spirit Warden' to 'Bloodthirsty Predators'. I like the Spirit World but I find that it detracts from the grittier, earthier elements of the game that I like - particularly the interpack politics, the conflict between ideologies, the struggle to maintain control of one's humanity, the gustatory need to hunt, and the danger one poses to one's inner circle.<br /> <br /> Here is a link to my work so far (it's still very much in progress). I'm taking parts of Werewolf the Forsaken that I like or that are evocative of the feeling I want (there's also some good writing in there that does a great job) and adding stuff of my own or making minor alterations, while including my own ideas. I'd also appreciate some of your own ideas, particularly for how to add a pervasive feeling of 'having something to do' that Forsaken invokes.<br /> <br /> Before anyone brings it up, I know that lots of people love the Spirit World and disagree with removing it. That's fine, I've heard the arguments both for and against, and I'd rather not revisit it. I'd greatly appreciate ideas to make things more interesting, more diversified, balance mechanics, and add a proper 'Main Foe' if you have ideas for them.<br /> <br /> I got the motivation to start this hack after reading 'Werewolf 2.0 Nine Ways it Could Be Streaminlined' : <a href=\"http://www.musoapbox.net/topic/270/werewolf-2-0-nine-ways-it-could-be-streamlined\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.musoapbox.net/topic/270/w...be-streamlined</a><br /> <br /> I went and made my own list of criticisms and improvements like any good imitator, which is in the doc. Here it is so that you can have an idea of what I've been going for before delving into the Hack itself, if you decide to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dr9klFe1InGiCGWHT22BmweFrMyBhQ3py2lbCMk-ImE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dr9klFe1InGiCGWHT22BmweFrMyBhQ3py2lbCMk-ImE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dr9klFe1InGiCGWHT22BmweFrMyBhQ3py2lbCMk-ImE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dr9klFe1InGiCGWHT22BmweFrMyBhQ3py2lbCMk-ImE/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Once again, all credit goes to all the artists, authors, producers, and others whose work inspired and went into this document. It's free for anyone's use and nobody is permitted to profit from it. The document is property of Viskarenvisla. <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Iceberg\">What is this</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I love Werewolf the Forsaken. It\u2019s a game with a lot of great themes, design elements, some very good storytelling potential, and a lot of really cool mechanics to demonstrate how it is to play a Werewolf. However, it\u2019s a game with lots of flaws that ultimately detract from the whole purpose of the story: being a Werewolf. To remedy this, I will excise the portions of Forsaken that I think are useless or detract from the game, and either leave them be or come up with replacements.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Iceberg\">What detracts from the game?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>The Spirit World</b>. I find the Shadow to be an alright concept but in the world of Werewolf it ultimately distracts from the feature of Werewolf I find to be most interesting - that of actually being a Werewolf. The game includes tons of content about the actual Shadow itself, how it should behave, what it should feel like, but it\u2019s often very difficult to put into play and doesn\u2019t support the game itself very well unless done very, very well. Spirits can often be kind of cartoony and feel more ephemeral than is satisfying - hunting spirits is probably the least interesting aspect of the game and doesn\u2019t make you feel like a monster, it makes you feel like a monster-rancher and like you\u2019re not very involved with the world around you. Moreover I find that the Shadow is a good reason to basically have anything happen - \u2018why is x/y/z this way? Oh because of the Shadow\u2019 and the explanation basically ends. I think that Werewolf can function just fine without the Shadow, there are plenty of elements to choose from the associated mythos to give the game a sense of weight and information density often associated with WoD games.</li> <li><b>Renown</b>. Renown served a good function when used in conjunction with gifts but at this point I think renown ties people down to certain behaviors, can be kind of arbitrary, doesn\u2019t explain how it lends more power to Werewolves, and is just another massive XP sink. Moreover if you don\u2019t decide to stick to one of the two presented factions - namely the Forsaken or the Pure - it\u2019s basically impossible to get renown, gimping you against other Uratha.</li> <li><b>Harmony</b>. In 2.0 Harmony served a function that I think becomes a statistical distraction - there are all these different rules associated with having your harmony be hither and yon, and with its effects on your ability to shapeshift, hop between the Hisil and Flesh, and the various bans, I think it essentially isn\u2019t very useful for telling a tale of savage horror. I actually liked 1.0 Harmony because it was a measure of your monstrosity vs. your humanity, which should be a central theme of Werewolf. If there needs to be some sort of morality scale within Werewolf, I think the 1.0 version can be tweaked.</li> <li><b>Spirit/Flesh Dualism</b>. The whole descent from a god and his little godling-wolves bit got very confusing. It generally ties in with the discomfort I had with the Spirit World in general, and is frankly less interesting than the Human/Beast dualism.</li> <li><b>Fetishes</b>. While I think that having magical items is a great idea in a game to add some more mechanical flavor and a few more tricks, the idea of a magical item having a spirit bound into it feels more cartoony than Werewolfy.</li> <li><b>Siskur-Dah</b>. I actually like the concept of marking your chosen prey or goal, but not with some booga-booga ritual. Having it tie in mechanically with cool gifts or features was a great idea, but the whole spirit booga made it less cool.</li> <li><b>Numerous Gifts</b>. There are quite a few gifts in the game which are either stupid or useless, and while the concept of gifts could be streamlined and made more interesting with their removal, their presence is still irritating. I\u2019m looking at you gender-flip gift.</li> <li><b>Tribes and Auspices</b>. Tribes and auspices are boring. They should enhance gameplay and give you a sense of quality and coolness that others outside your tribe lack, but I find them to be half-assed in their approach to taking on a specific prey. Forsaken tried to solve the ethnic butterfly problem that Apocalypse had, but generally speaking the tribes pigeonhole characters and don\u2019t add much. Moreover, how is it that Blood Talons in India and Australia have so much in common? Oh of course, \u201cthe Spirit World\u201d, silly me. Their only real benefit is mechanical, and it\u2019s an unnecessary one. Auspices feel like classes from DnD too, and while I can appreciate the logic I think it is unfit for this type of game.</li> <li><b>Wolf-Bloods</b>. I understand the logic here with White Wolf trying to standardize everything - vampires have ghouls, werewolves have wolfbloods, mages have acolytes, etc., but again I think that they just don\u2019t fit in very well with the overall style and feel of Werewolf. They offer kind of a cop-out to the difficulty of dealing with humanity and whom you let close. However, I do believe that the idea of being able to infuse a human with Werewolf power in some way and bind them to your will is a cool idea worth exploring.</li> <li><b>Dalu and Urshul</b>. I think that the impact of shapeshifting is increased if there are less forms. The Dalu and Urshul allow more leeway in the Hunt, and I think that decreasing the number of forms means that the other forms are more impactful, important, and decisive - some of the traits of the other forms, like Badass Motherfucker or inflicting Tilts, can be bought as Manifestations for the various forms.</li> <li><b>Eat Spirits, not People</b>. I mean...fine, I get it. Eating people definitely pushes the boundary here but if we\u2019re going for a game that brings savage horror to the forefront, I think eating people would definitely do it AND add an element of care to the game that a lot of werewolves can simply avoid by sticking to spirits and animals as prey. Spirits are too weird and alien to function as edible prey and again detracts from the Werewolf experience, while the other various monsters of the game like Hosts, Vampires, Humans, and other Werewolves, in my opinion, make fantastic prey.</li> <li><b>Limited Factions</b>. Okay so there\u2019s Forsaken and Pure. That\u2019s it. Everything else is negligible and unimportant in the grand scheme of things. While the Forsaken are kinda whatever and uninteresting, I find that there is great potential in the Pure as a faction, since they represent the most extreme, uncontrolled aspects of being a Werewolf.</li> </ol><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Iceberg\">What Would Add to the Game?</span></span></b><br /><br /><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>No Spirit World</b>. Just get rid of it. It\u2019s not necessary in my opinion. I think an element of supernatural mystery can definitely be attained with implications that Luna is some sort of mad goddess, and that there may be some ghostly <i>things</i> that can mess with Werewolves but this shouldn\u2019t be a primary focus. The idea of being a spirit-cop got old really fast - the Werewolf condition itself is a great source of power and possibility.</li> <li><b>The Change as Curse/Disease</b>. Being Uratha is often seen as some sort of blessing mixed with a few negatives - I\u2019d rather balance them out, and not only that, I\u2019d like it to be a Curse that can be transmittable, a la the whole \u2018bitten by a werewolf, become a werewolf\u2019 trope. I think that this would be the core change that I\u2019d make for this game, changing the focus of the condition and its source of power from a blessing from the Spirit World into a strange, otherworldly Curse or possibly a Disease that afflicts soul and body, changing the bearer into a ravaging monster that hungers for the flesh of other predators. The Curse itself is mysterious and unexplained - it seems to be partially hereditary, mostly inflicted, and ultimately its source is difficult to pin down, with multiple conflicting tales, steeped in superstition and mired in mistruths and legend. There are numerous \u2018primogenitors\u2019 of the various Strains that seem to have cropped up in history, with few shared features - some have been horrible monsters, some have been saintly, some have been simple, normal people, but ultimately unless they have died without passing on the Curse, they create their own Strain of Lycanthropy. As the Curse defies the laws of physics not just in allowing spontaneous generation of matter, high-speed regeneration, and monstrous strength, it also allows for numerous anomalous abilities that aren\u2019t usually accounted for in the tales, giving Werewolves particular edges. Basically, a Werewolf is created when someone in the War-Form bites a mortal and they survive to Change.<br /> <br /> In this way, I am very much stealing from Vampire, whose backstory in both Masquerade and Requiem I think are very good. The mystery and lack of clarity about the condition are far more tantalizing than the way things are basically completely laid out in Forsaken or Apocalypse.</li> <li><b>Better gifts</b>. A lot of gifts are useless. This was especially pronounced in 1.0 but I still believe that 2.0\u2019s gifts leave a lot to be desired. Moreover they are often magicky to the point that it doesn\u2019t really fit in well with the Werewolf mythos, which I think should rely less on outward magic and more on biological/curse/subtle themes, and without the Spirit World this can be done much more easily. Ideally, this edit will so do away with things like gifts of the Elements, which were poorly defined since they relied on a poorly defined attribute (spirit influence).</li> <li><b>Customizable Forms - Manifestations</b>. This is a test idea and I\u2019m not sure how it\u2019ll work out, but I think that it might be worth giving a try. I got it from Demon the Fallen, and I really liked the way your Apocalyptic Form could be so readily changeable. Rather than sinking XP into renown, which may grant gifts and be used in various dice rolls, I think it\u2019d be cooler to instead be able to emphasize the sheer mercurial nature of Uratha and be able to change aspects of the War Form. Depending on your Primal Urge, you can have additional Manifestations that the player themselves can create. How are these different from gifts? Gifts you have to spend Rage on and tend to have bigger, more complicated effects; Manifestations are static bonuses or tricks you can use in your forms. You can switch them out at will once they\u2019ve been purchased for XP, and STs and Players should work together to create their own Manifestations.</li> <li><b>Strains Replacing Tribes</b>. I think that the more diversity there is in a game the better. One of the problems with the CoD series is that they try to compact everything into a few splats like Tribe and Auspice or Clan and Covenant, or whatever. Since these are savage beasts without a Spirit World to unite them, there is endless variance in ideology - we\u2019ll be focusing on the American continent, where there are definitely quite a few different unique Strains, some with extremely ancient roots in Native American myth, some with their origins in Continental Europe and Africa. Strains will also give a tangible, real mechanical benefit as well as a certain amount of definition to just how the Curse manifests. Players and STs should definitely work to create their own Strains as they see fit.</li> <li><b>Primal Urge as Power+ Stat</b>. One thing I liked about Primal Urge was that it did a number of good things for you in Werewolf 2.0 - increased your Rage and how much you could use per round, added to your time in Gauru, increased the potency of some gifts, and made it so you had to consume particular kinds of prey to stay functioning. Now by getting rid of Renown Primal Urge will instead function in its place, granting increased power to Gifts and maybe some Manifestations as well. Primal Urge is not increased through XP - instead it is increased through milestones of interacting with the Change, succeeding in particular Hunts, taking down certain Prey, living through certain disastrous events and coming through them...some milestones will be decided upon by the Players and ST.</li> <li><b>Enthralled</b>. These would replace Wolfbloods. Rather than having relatives or family that are kinda pseudo-werewolves, you can instead, kind of like Demons or Vampires, pass on a measure of your Curse to normal humans and tie them to your will. This can be done through intense, close interactions, such as sexuality, deep personal relationship, transmitting part of the Curse through a bite, and persistent haunting. This way the Uratha can in fact pass one of their Manifestations on to an Enthralled - further subjugation can add another Manifestation, but it runs the risk of inflicting The Curse wholesale and creating another Werewolf.</li> <li><b>Numerous Factions</b>. Rather than just Pure or Forsaken, which had enormous bearing on your progression and the kind of character you could play, I will introduce a number of possible factions that will be somewhat more like philosophical/creed organizations, rather like those in Mage or Vampire. Some war with each other for control of hunting grounds, establishing rules of dominance or trying to impose certain laws upon their fellows. Some are wide-ranging networks that can span entire states - some go no further than a particular neighborhood.</li> <li><b>Marking Prey</b>. I liked the idea of <i>Siskur-Dah</i> but I didn\u2019t like how it was carried out. The Chosen Prey of a Werewolf, however, can still be selected and marked with the same benefits of <i>Siskur-Dah</i>. In order to Mark Prey, one must interact with them similarly to Enthrallment, but usually a single bite with the intent to mark the prey is sufficient. If the prey is a particular goal rather than a thing, some sort of small ritual may need to be done, to be tested and seen how it functions.</li> <li><b>Magic Items but how?</b> I think that these are important for mechanics and rewards, but how would I implement them???</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T20:47:10-07:00","id":1237005,"title":"","content":"Haven\u2019t read the whole thing yet, but at a glance the whole looks more like a 2E Wolf-Blooded game with ramped up powers rather than an alternate Forsaken game. Or perhaps a Changing Breeds (nWoD) game without the sexual fetishism of animals and anti-civilization stuff. Will have to read further though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T20:59:45-07:00","id":1237008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1237002-2e-setting-hack-werewolf-the-curse?p=1237005#post1237005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haven\u2019t read the whole thing yet, but at a glance the whole looks more like a 2E Wolf-Blooded game with ramped up powers rather than an alternate Forsaken game. Or perhaps a Changing Breeds (nWoD) game without the sexual fetishism of animals and anti-civilization stuff. Will have to read further though.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of the presented issues frankly sound like they'd be better managed by either leaning into what 2e already offers for high-Harmony games or playing a fleshier reskin of Vampire instead \u2014 part of the way that Werewolf's whole particular secret world angle fits in with conventional werewolf stories is as a means for werewolves to <i>mitigate</i> the problems that media often focuses on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T21:32:08-07:00","id":1237016,"title":"","content":"Read a bit more deeper now (but not enough yet!). It seems not all but most of the issues revolve around the werewolves\u2019 spirituality. If so, then removing it is a solution, though I imagine the results won\u2019t be much popular. <br /> <br /> And I\u2019ll be stealing the ideas for a nWoD/1E Changing Breeds reboot to 2E/CofD, if you don\u2019t mind!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T21:46:26-07:00","id":1237020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>viskarenvisla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1237002-2e-setting-hack-werewolf-the-curse#post1237002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Marking Prey</b>. I liked the idea of <i>Siskur-Dah</i> but I didn\u2019t like how it was carried out. The Chosen Prey of a Werewolf, however, can still be selected and marked with the same benefits of <i>Siskur-Dah</i>. In order to Mark Prey, one must interact with them similarly to Enthrallment, but usually a single bite with the intent to mark the prey is sufficient. If the prey is a particular goal rather than a thing, some sort of small ritual may need to be done, to be tested and seen how it functions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've actually seen this suggested before, though I have no idea if it was you who suggested it, and I have the same question. My werewolf is in the same location as Victim. My werewolf bites Victim. Why is there any length of time between this and the moment my werewolf kills victim? What is a hunt, when the prey is literally in your mouth?<br /> <br /> Aside from the previous mention of wolf-blooded, you might look at the <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/92398/Forsaken-Chroniclers-Guide\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicler's Guide</a>, specifically part 4, the Family section. It 'removes tribe, Auspice, Gifts, Rites, and most everything else from Forsaken existence, along with the Shadow and most aspects of the condition. In the wake of all that removal, we leave the pack as the sole organization and interest of the Forsaken. This allows for complex systems of trust and betrayal to drive the game.'<br /> <br /> It doesn't completely remove tribes but changes them to reflect a character's outlook on existence as a werewolf (what second edition did), with the 'tribes' being alphas, shepherds, sages, stalkers, and warriors.<br /> <br /> Or <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Beast:_The_Primordial\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a>, which might be the kind of thing you're looking for. One can play a game of 'werewolf' in it and not involve the shadow or other supernaturals at all, instead playing a game about stalking human prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-20-2018, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T05:35:20-07:00","id":1237101,"title":"","content":"I still need to read more, but this looks similar to one apocalypse (end of the old world, not the WoD gameline) idea I had - Iron Gauntlet. That basically had it where the Gauntlet became near impenetrable, locking out most of the Shadow and its influence. Loci largely dried up, and so what is the other major source of Essence? This was back before Werewolf 2E, though, so the harsh consequences to Harmony were more direct.<br /> <br /> Just looking over your summary for now, <br /> 1. I'd retain at least <i>some</i> of the Spirit World, just cut the overwhelming focus and influence. Leaving it in, but rare and optional lets you use (even as a red-herring) the idea of &quot;wolf-spirit-possession&quot; being a mechanism behind the curse. Which might have some nice tie-on elements. It also lets you have have things like Vision Quests, and Totem Spirits, but keep it optional - not every pack might have one. Dial between &quot;Many&quot; and &quot;Rare&quot; as you choose. Basically just leverage the Spirit as an optional backing for whatever magic-like-stuff you may need in the background and ignore it otherwise.<br /> 3. Since most of the 2E Gifts directly interact with the Spirit, Wolf, or Hunter part of Werewolves, just keep the ones that are thematic, let them buy them individually, and recast them as personally developments/transformations instead of &quot;Gifts&quot;.<br /> 7. This sounds frankly like an attempt at copying Ghouls directly. I suggest just leaving Wolf-blooded as is. They are people that have some genetic tie to Werewolves, which manifests in their own curse and one-off abilities. For &quot;late-bloomer&quot; or &quot;inflicted&quot; Wolf-Blooded, just say that they have a resistance to the Curse, so it doesn't fully manifest.<br /> 9. I suggest you leverage the heavy focus on the Pack in 2E. Instead of Shadow-Bestowed-or-manipulating-Rites, have the various ad-hoc activities and rituals a pack conducts act as a sort of psychic gestalt lens. Stuff happens (like supernaturally marking prey) because enough people united in one will <i>decide</i> it happens. Think of it like the Pack all metaphysically howling &quot;We are coming for <i>you</i>.&quot; If you want to completely cut out the Spirit, you can use that for any magic-like stuff you need too.<br /> 10. See above for either lingering Spirit influence, psychic-gestalt (strong enough impression might &quot;stain&quot; an item), or just shrug. Before Mummy, Relics just &quot;happened&quot;, so why bother to give rando-magic-items a common explanation.<br /> <br /> Some thoughts:<br /> \u2022 [Wolf-Spirit] If you are representing the Curse as being &quot;possessed-by-wolf-spirit&quot;, they Harmony might be similar to 1E Synergy in concept (two parties being able to work together) and 2E Clarity mechanically (working like a damage track, with differing levels of infractions causing lingering but recoverable harm). Alternatively, you could ditch it entirely as a numeric track and instead use Conditions like Harmony, Disharmony, Conflicted, Berserk, Fugue, etc. They could lead back and forth between each other, or whatever other level of interaction you prefer.<br /> \u2022 [Wolf-Spirit] For passing on the Curse via bite, you might look at some representations of the &quot;Join-or-be-prey&quot; aspects of the Wild Hunt. Specifically, when a Werewolf on the Hunt bites a target, they subconsciously choose - Fight, Flee, or Join. The prior two are obvious, but the last one means the &quot;victim&quot; has decided to accept a &quot;wolf&quot; inside them too, and become a werewolf (over time).<br /> \u2022 You might exchange Essence for Hunger, either as a simple renaming, or treating it like an inverse track. Or even trading it for Conditions, with expenditures either automatically swapping them for &quot;hungrier&quot; Conditions, or rolling to risk &quot;getting Hungry&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T07:09:13-07:00","id":1237128,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for taking the time to address my questions and look upon my creation. Let us consider each one in turn:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1237002-2e-setting-hack-werewolf-the-curse?p=1237008#post1237008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of the presented issues frankly sound like they'd be better managed by either leaning into what 2e already offers for high-Harmony games or playing a fleshier reskin of Vampire instead \u2014 part of the way that Werewolf's whole particular secret world angle fits in with conventional werewolf stories is as a means for werewolves to <i>mitigate</i> the problems that media often focuses on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you go more into detail here and give me some examples? I don't quite follow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T07:36:46-07:00","id":1237136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>viskarenvisla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1237002-2e-setting-hack-werewolf-the-curse?p=1237128#post1237128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you go more into detail here and give me some examples? I don't quite follow.</div> </div> </div> </div>A character with no access to the Sacred Hunt rite loses Essence daily and makes breaking points away from the spirit, both of which make shapeshifting and accessing the Shadow harder and encourage you to eat people to try and rebalance. The game already provides multiple core Merits for customizing your forms and at least one Merit specific to high-Harmony werewolves. You'll likely lean closer to ritualistic hunters than shapeshifting shamans in this mode, with a greater emphasis on rites and Merits over Gifts <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, things you want like more factions, an increased emphasis on Man Versus Beast, customizable forms, lycanthropy as a contagious affliction, and so on are already amply represented by Requiem's mechanics for Feeding Grounds, Kindred Senses, frenzy, Protean, and the like. It's less work making vampirism not involve you being dead than it is to carve out a separate niche for werewolves than the one built on cultural touchstones like hunting and animism and community.<br /> <br /> Tangentially: Back off on the derision present in the OP going forward, please, because it's not doing you any favors to call the Shadow &quot;cartoony&quot; or Luna's Embrace &quot;stupid [and] irritating.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-20-2018, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T07:53:11-07:00","id":1237143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1237002-2e-setting-hack-werewolf-the-curse?p=1237020#post1237020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've actually seen this suggested before, though I have no idea if it was you who suggested it, and I have the same question. My werewolf is in the same location as Victim. My werewolf bites Victim. Why is there any length of time between this and the moment my werewolf kills victim? What is a hunt, when the prey is literally in your mouth?<br /> <br /> Aside from the previous mention of wolf-blooded, you might look at the <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://drivethrurpg.com/product/92398/Forsaken-Chroniclers-Guide&amp;quot;]Chronicler's</a> Guide[/URL], specifically part 4, the Family section. It 'removes tribe, Auspice, Gifts, Rites, and most everything else from Forsaken existence, along with the Shadow and most aspects of the condition. In the wake of all that removal, we leave the pack as the sole organization and interest of the Forsaken. This allows for complex systems of trust and betrayal to drive the game.'<br /> <br /> It doesn't completely remove tribes but changes them to reflect a character's outlook on existence as a werewolf (what second edition did), with the 'tribes' being alphas, shepherds, sages, stalkers, and warriors.<br /> <br /> Or <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Beast:_The_Primordial&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a>, which might be the kind of thing you're looking for. One can play a game of 'werewolf' in it and not involve the shadow or other supernaturals at all, instead playing a game about stalking human prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a really good point. Why wouldn't that be the case? It's just movie suspense that allows for someone to get bit and end up being stalked for the most part.<br /> <br /> I think that I need to reconsider the Marked Prey mechanic, maybe on the same lines as what Vent0 suggested. The Curse is this mutative, malignant effect that takes place upon objective reality, and werewolves in a pack have a gestalt influence by however it is they choose to affirm reality - some perform a ritual like in 2e, some simply make a solemn announcement, some write it down on a 'master list'.<br /> <br /> Any ideas you have for a sort of 'game antagonist' a la spirits or Anshega is welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T08:06:55-07:00","id":1237148,"title":"","content":"The Hosts can be reintroduced as purely \u2018physical\u2019 monstrosities. In fact, it\u2019d be easier than changing the werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T08:16:50-07:00","id":1237152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1237002-2e-setting-hack-werewolf-the-curse?p=1237136#post1237136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tangentially: Back off on the derision present in the OP going forward, please, because it's not doing you any favors to call the Shadow &amp;quot;cartoony&amp;quot; or Luna's Embrace &amp;quot;stupid [and] irritating.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I second that. Wholeheartedly! So much in fact, that I think the Tone actively harms you, putting people off of helping you out, e.g. me.<br /> The Tone was enough to entirely put me off of this idea (which in and of itself is fine) because I constantly found myself saying &quot;No it is not&quot;, &quot;I disagree&quot;, &quot;I could say the same about your approach&quot;, &quot;that would make it bland and boring&quot; and &quot;That is what makes the setting so interesting!&quot;, Growing Increasingly frustrated with what seemed to me like you missed the point of the game.<br /> Try and Phrase it so that those things are your opinion, rather Than Pass Them Off as objective fact.<br /> <br /> I also have to agree with Satchel regarding reworking Vampire into a Werewolf game rather than going with Werewolf, because the themes you are looking for are, ironically, more present there. It will be less work all in all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T10:32:13-07:00","id":1237188,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Closed by OP request.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}